    {
      "text": "let us build us a city and a tower, Gen. 11:4. build me an house for me to dwell, 2 Sam. 7:5 (1 Chr. 17:4). David … to build an house for the name of the Lord, 1 Kgs. 8:17 (2 Chr. 6:7). He shall build an house for my name, 1 Chr. 22:10. he hath charged me to build him an house in Jerusalem, 2 Chr. 36:23. let us build up the wall of Jerusalem, Neh. 2:17. build thou the walls of Jerusalem, Ps. 51:18. Except the Lord build the house, they labour in vain that build it, Ps. 127:1. wise woman buildeth her house, Prov. 14:1. Through wisdom is an house builded, Prov. 24:3. a time to break down, and a time to build up, Eccl. 3:3. he shall build my city, Isa. 45:13. shall build the old waste places, Isa. 58:12 (61:4). I have … set thee over the nations … to build, and to plant, Jer. 1:10. I will build them, and not pull them down, Jer. 24:6. I will build thee, and thou shalt be built, Jer. 31:4. to return, and will build them, as at the first, Jer. 33:7. still abide in this land, then will I build you, Jer. 42:10. I the Lord build the ruined places, Ezek. 36:36. tabernacle of David … I will build it, Amos 9:11. They build up Zion with blood, Micah 3:10. the time that the Lord’s house should be built, Hag. 1:2. he shall build the temple of the Lord, Zech. 6:12. They shall build, but I will throw down, Mal. 1:4.",
